```suggestion
            if (hasUrl || hasToken) {
              console.info('ℹ️  Found transfer configuration in your environment:');
              if (hasUrl) {
                console.info('   → STRAPI_TRANSFER_URL environment variable value will be used as default URL');
              }
              if(hasToken) {
                console.info('   → STRAPI_TRANSFER_TOKEN environment variable value will be used as default token');
              }
```

I found this a little confusing/distracting when I was testing it. If I only set one of the two, I don't expect to see the other, and my brain doesn't want to read all that but is forced to to find out why there's something I didn't set, it felt like something went wrong 😆 For me, I'd prefer to just see the item that I set.

If we do want to keep it this way, maybe we could make the "found" items green or something and the not-found items yellow or something?

Shouldn't this be

```typescript
if (opts.from) {
  return 'from';
}
if (opts.to) {
  return 'to';
}
```

Right now if I do `strapi transfer --from [URL] --from-token [TOKEN]` it still asks me about a URL and token, and the direction message on line 134 also says 'send data to', because the `direction` will be set to my `--from` URL instead of to the string `'from'`.
